WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.120
In Episode 4 of “What If…?,” we see something&nbsp;
we haven’t seen in the series thus far.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:10.000
The story revolves around Dr. Steven Strange&nbsp;
and his love interest, Dr. Christine Palmer.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:14.240
From the get-go, it’s obvious this world is&nbsp;
different than the one we know from the MCU&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.840
as Steven is head-over-heels in&nbsp;
love with Christine. In “Doctor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.480
Strange,” it’s evident there&nbsp;
are feelings between the two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:25.360
but Steven’s ego and narcissism often prevent&nbsp;
their love from blossoming. In Episode 4,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:30.240
the duo appears to have genuine passion between&nbsp;
them, which isn’t hindered by his cockiness.

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:35.280
The episode begins with the duo taking a ride in&nbsp;
Steven’s car. After some chit-chat, it looks like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.680
they’re about to be in a terrible car crash,&nbsp;
but Steven is able to maneuver his sports car,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.840
so they avoid the accident. Unfortunately,&nbsp;
they’re hit by another vehicle from behind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:48.640
which sends them spiraling off the road.&nbsp;
The accident is reminiscent of Steven’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.960
from the character’s live-action film; the&nbsp;
difference is, this time, he's not alone.

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.640
Christine dies in the crash,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.160
and the Watcher tells us how this universe&nbsp;
is different from the one we know:

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:05.440
"In this universe, Steven Strange&nbsp;
didn't lose his hands, but his heart."

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:10.400
Just like in “Doctor Strange,” Steven still&nbsp;
travels to the Kamar-Taj, where he learns about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:15.040
the mystic arts as he seeks answers to help deal&nbsp;
with his grief. He experiments with the Eye of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.320
Agamotto as he learns time travel is possible&nbsp;
but is warned by Wong to not tinker with it.

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:24.240
"Tinkering with time can weaken&nbsp;
the very fabric of the universe.”

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.400
The episode speeds over the death of the&nbsp;
Ancient One and Steven’s defeat of Dormammu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.200
as he becomes the Sorcerer Supreme. It&nbsp;
also leaves out Baron Mordo entirely,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:37.840
a character essential to the plot in the “Doctor&nbsp;
Strange” film. While these events fall in line&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:43.040
with the ones we’ve seen in the MCU, what happens&nbsp;
next is a complete left turn from what we know.

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:47.440
Steven is still unable to deal with the&nbsp;
loss of Christine two years after her death.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:52.240
He uses the Eye of Agamotto to travel back to&nbsp;
the night of their car accident and maneuvers his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.840
vehicle differently to avoid the same crash. While&nbsp;
he’s successful, they’re still hit by another car&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:03.040
in an entirely different accident and land in&nbsp;
the same spot, resulting in Christine’s death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:08.640
yet again. Steven continues to turn back time&nbsp;
over and over — drastically changing the events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:13.840
of the evening to prevent tragedy. But no matter&nbsp;
what he does, Christine dies every single time.

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:18.880
It’s here we learn from the Ancient One that&nbsp;
Christine’s death is an “absolute point in time.”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.240
She explains that without the death of his&nbsp;
loved one, he would never have mastered the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:27.920
mystic arts or defeated Dormammu, suggesting&nbsp;
her death is necessary to save the universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:31.760
Steven won’t accept this and goes down a&nbsp;
dangerous path of attempting to reverse&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.560
this absolute point in time. He seeks&nbsp;
answers at the Lost Library of Cagliostro.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:39.840
Steven learns at the library that he&nbsp;
can obtain the power to reverse an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.640
absolute point by gaining the power of other&nbsp;
beings through absorption. His dark path takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:49.280
an even darker turn as he summons mythical&nbsp;
beings just so he can absorb their powers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.240
Steven becomes incredibly strong, even&nbsp;
prompting the Watcher to consider intervening.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:58.480
Soon, we cut back to an earlier point in the&nbsp;
episode just after Doctor Strange defeats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:03.120
Dormammu — the moment just before Steven&nbsp;
reverts time. He puts off his time travel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:08.080
and when he goes outside, he sees his reality&nbsp;
slowly starting to wither away as buildings and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.800
people appear to disintegrate. The Ancient One&nbsp;
shows up again, and we learn of a new twist.

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.040
It turns out, the Ancient One split&nbsp;
reality into two timelines the moment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:21.920
Steven used the Eye of Agamotto to travel&nbsp;
back in time using dark magic. This allowed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.560
two Stevens to simultaneously exist in one&nbsp;
universe, and shortly after learning this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:30.880
the Doctor Stranges come face to face.&nbsp;
One fights for the sake of the universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:34.880
and the other fights to save Christine&nbsp;
by reversing that absolute point in time.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:40.240
It’s a brutal battle between the two, with dark&nbsp;
Steven coming out victorious as he absorbs the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.640
power of his counterpart. He is successful&nbsp;
in stopping Christine’s death that night,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:49.840
but that choice ends up decimating the entire&nbsp;
universe. Steven learns too late that reversing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:55.120
Christine’s death changes everything, and in this&nbsp;
new reality everything crumbles and he loses his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.160
love yet again. Steven talks to the Watcher&nbsp;
as the universe disintegrates and admits he’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.120
always felt his presence. In a last-ditch effort,&nbsp;
he begs him to intervene and to set things right.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:11.040
"You, you can stop this. Please, fix this."

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:15.440
But the Watcher refuses, saying that&nbsp;
interfering with time and events only&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:20.320
leads to further destruction, so he watches the&nbsp;
world crumble as Steven and Christine perish.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:26.000
As we learned in the three episodes prior, one&nbsp;
decision can change absolutely everything. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.720
Episode 4, it’s more evident than ever as the&nbsp;
Watcher explains that these choices can destroy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.720 --> 00:04:35.840
the entire universe. Clearly, some choices bear&nbsp;
more weight than others. Steven’s response to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:40.240
losing the use of his hands in “Doctor Strange”&nbsp;
was substantially different from the reaction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:45.120
he had to the death of Christine. Both stories&nbsp;
saw him triumph against Dormammu and become the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.120 --> 00:04:48.960
Sorcerer Supreme, but his partner’s&nbsp;
death was too much for him to bear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.400
which led to all-out destruction&nbsp;
through his always evident arrogance.

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:56.800
While the difference in this story was Christine’s&nbsp;
death over the destruction of his hands, it was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.800 --> 00:05:02.160
ultimately Steven’s decision to reverse that&nbsp;
absolute point in time which ended the universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:06.480
We’re still left wondering will the Watcher&nbsp;
ever intervene? This is the most we’ve seen him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:11.360
interact with a story thus far, but if he wouldn’t&nbsp;
intervene as the universe was being destroyed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:14.880
what situation might we see that would&nbsp;
force him to step in and do something?

